{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>האמרת.</b> From the expression of greatness and closeness, from the root ראש אמיר ויאמר. And Rabbi Judah Halevi the Spaniard, may his memory be for a blessing, said that the word is from the root ויאמר, and the meaning is that you have done what is right until He says that He will be your Elohim, and He too does for you until you said that you will be to Him for a treasured people. And he explained well. And so האמרת is a verb with two objects."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The phrase 'מגזרת בראש אמיר ויאמר' is opaque; translated hyper-literally. נ״ע expanded to 'may his memory be for a blessing' by convention."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:25:01.145769715Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}